  {
   "id": 367579,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure class=\"unnumbered\">\n<img src=\"exercises/media/c5596493d9da285e.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n<figcaption>(credit: modification of work by Cornelia M Spies, et al./<i>Arthritis Research &amp; Therapy</i>, under CC BY 4.0 license)</figcaption>\n</figure>\n",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal (HPA) axis, one of the major components of the endocrine system, during inflammation.</p>\n<p>Which statement describes the role of cortisol in this system?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 891536,
     "content_html": "Triggering metabolic effects against inflammation and increasing the production of CRH and ACTH."
    },
    {
     "id": 891537,
     "content_html": "Triggering metabolic effects against inflammation and decreasing the production of CRH and ACTH."
    },
    {
     "id": 891538,
     "content_html": "Increasing the production of CRH and decreasing the production of ACTH."
    },
    {
     "id": 891539,
     "content_html": "Increasing the production of ACTH and decreasing the production of CRH."
    }
   ],
